# Run 387 evidence archive — only README.md, summary.txt, and .gitignore are tracked.
# Everything else here is verify/CI-artifact-only or per-run temporary output and MUST NOT be committed.
# In particular NO attestation blob, signature, OIDC token, or signing-key material is ever committed:
# the real build-provenance attestation is minted only by the disabled-by-default protected workflow
# .github/workflows/public-devnet-release-signing-attestation.yml and lives in GitHub's attestation
# store, never in the repository. Only the publish-safe attestation IDENTITY summary
# (ATTESTATION_IDENTITY.txt) and status lines are ever surfaced, and even those stay CI-artifact-only
# except for the tracked README.md/summary.txt. The generated RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.json remains a
# CI *artifact* (uploaded by the Run 385/386 workflows), never a committed changing file; the committed,
# publish-safe example manifest lives at docs/release/public-devnet/binary/RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.example.json.
# Node data dirs, node logs, raw /metrics scrape dumps, the staged ci-artifacts/ bundle, any built binary,
# and reused Run 385/386 outputs are temporary and dev/CI-only.
ci-artifacts/
run385/
run386/
node-data/
nodes/
logs/
data/
qbind-node
qbind-node.sha256
RELEASE_ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.json
manifest.json
BUILDID.txt
SIGNING_PREFLIGHT.txt
MANIFEST_VALIDATION_SUMMARY.txt
ATTESTATION_IDENTITY.txt
*.sig
*.sigstore
*.sigstore.json
*.intoto.jsonl
*.dsse
*.attestation
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jwt
*.oidc
clean_metrics.txt
metrics.txt
*.metrics
*.err
*.log
*.metrics.txt
manifest.metrics.txt